findings.proof_of_concept:
function test_reentrancy_claimPlenty_crossFunction() public {
    // Setup: whitelist a Well whose non-Bean token is a hook-bearing ERC-777-style token.
    // Accrue plenty to attacker via a Flood (sop) so perWellPlenty[well].plenty > 0.
    // Action: attacker (EOA -> attacker contract) calls claimPlenty(well, To.EXTERNAL).
    //   During sopToken.safeTransfer at ClaimFacet.sol#100, the token's tokensReceived/
    //   transfer hook re-enters Beanstalk via fillPodOrder()/claimFertilized() (no nonReentrant).
    // Assert L2 state-flip: read perWellPlenty[well].plenty == old value DURING the hook (vm.load);
    //   confirm reentered market/fert call observes pre-zeroed plenty and non-decremented
    //   plentyPerSopToken[sopToken].
    // Assert L3: measure whether the combined reentry can leave protocol balance < entitlement
    //   AFTER the outer fundsSafu runs. If fundsSafu reverts, finding is bounded to Medium hazard.
}

