findings.proof_of_concept:
function test_reentrancy_cancelPodOrder_sendBeforeDelete() public {
    // L1: create a pod order escrowing Bean (podOrders[id] = X).
    // Demonstrate the ordering hazard: in _cancelPodOrder the send (Order.sol#137) precedes
    //   delete podOrders[id] (Order.sol#138). With Bean (no hook) the recipient gets no callback,
    //   so reentry is impossible -> test documents that the guard is the token's hooklessness,
    //   not the code ordering.
    // L2: if hooks were possible, assert podOrders[id] still == X during the recipient callback (vm.load).
    // L3: prove double-refund only under a hypothetical hook-bearing payout token (not Bean).
}

